{number: 67}
{title: Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Pass me not, O gentle Savior,
[F] Hear my humble [C] cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
[G7] Do not pass me [C] by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Savior, Savior,
[F] Hear my humble [C] cry;
While on others Thou art calling,
[G7] Do not pass me [C] by.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Let me at a throne of mercy
[F] Find a sweet re-[C] lief;
Kneeling there in deep contrition,
[G7] Help my unbe-[C] lief.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Trusting only in Thy merit,
[F] Would I seek Thy [C] face;
Heal my wounded, broken spirit,
[G7] Save me by Thy [C] grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Thou the Spring of all my comfort,
[F] More than life to [C] me,
Whom have I on earth beside Thee?
[G7] Whom in heav'n but [C] Thee?
{end_of_verse}
